In `@tools/sap-adt-mcp-launcher/src/config.ts` around lines 100 - 104, The option
parsers that use the inline handler signature (_arg, argv, i, s) currently do
argv[++i]! and immediately call toLowerCase(), which will throw or set undefined
for trailing options like --import-from, --workspace, and --destination; update
each handler (the ones handling --import-from referencing IMPORT_FROM_MODES, and
the handlers for --workspace and --destination) to first check that argv[i+1]
exists and is a string before incrementing i, return/throw a clear error like
"Missing value for --import-from" (or the specific option) when absent, avoid
the non-null assertion (!) and only call toLowerCase() on a validated string,
and then validate against IMPORT_FROM_MODES or assign into state as appropriate.
```

