_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Keep the incoming request when the pending queue overflows.**

When the queue is full, this branch shifts the oldest body and returns before `message.body` is appended. That drops the newest request instead of retaining it, so the bridge silently loses the client’s latest request while reporting the *oldest* one as evicted.

<details>
<summary>💡 Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
   enqueueOrDrop(message: McpStdioMessage): McpStdioMessage | undefined {
-    if (this.bodies.length >= this.limit) {
-      const shifted = this.bodies.shift();
-      if (shifted === undefined) return undefined;
-      return new McpStdioMessage(shifted);
-    }
+    let dropped: McpStdioMessage | undefined;
+    if (this.bodies.length >= this.limit) {
+      const shifted = this.bodies.shift();
+      if (shifted !== undefined) {
+        dropped = new McpStdioMessage(shifted);
+      }
+    }
     this.bodies.push(message.body);
-    return undefined;
+    return dropped;
   }
```
</details>

